  "query": "How do I make a grilled cheese sandwich?",
  "goal": {
    "title": "Pan-toast a cheese sandwich and serve it",
    "description": "Place two bread slices on a plate and remove a slice of marbled cheese from its packet. Open the spread tub and spread the pale spread over both bread slices with a knife. Put one bread slice in a frying pan, layer the cheese and the second slice on it, and turn on the gas burner. Wait, check the underside repeatedly with a spatula, flip and press the sandwich, then transfer the browned sandwich to the plate. Carry it to the island, wait and take a bite.",
    "final_state": "A browned cheese sandwich is served on the green plate and lifted for a bite.",
    "procedure": [
      "Set out bread and remove a cheese slice from its packet.",
      "Spread both bread slices with the tub spread.",
      "Layer bread, cheese and bread in the frying pan and light the burner.",
      "Cook the sandwich, checking and flipping it with the spatula.",
      "Transfer the sandwich to a plate, carry it to the island and taste it."
    ]
  },
